# SploitAgent ships the skills, not your engagement data.
# If you run engagements from a clone, keep findings/loot/notes local.

# --- Engagement working data (any engagement dir you create here) ---
engagements/
**/loot/
**/screenshots/
**/hosts/
**/chains/
**/findings/
scope.txt
roe.md
notes.md
state.md
deadends.md
report.md
report.json
*.pcap
*.hashes
*.creds
*.ccache
*.kirbi
*.nmap
*.gnmap

# Re-include the library itself (engagement-data patterns above must never hide skills/)
!skills/
!skills/**

# Re-include the project's own doc screenshots (the **/screenshots/ rule is for engagement data)
!docs/screenshots/
!docs/screenshots/**

# --- Secrets / local config ---
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*_id_rsa*

# --- Generated (regenerated by tools/catalog.py) ---
data/skills_index.json

# --- Benchmark harness (bench/) — downloaded target + run output, kept local ---
bench/.targets/
bench/runs/

# --- OS / editor junk ---
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
